# ZONE 1 — EXPERIENCE LAYER

## Web App (ReactJS)

Frontend application where users interact with AI, dashboards, reports, workflows, and conversational interfaces.

---

## Responsive UI

Ensures seamless user experience across desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.

---

## Personalization

Customizes AI responses, dashboards, recommendations, and user experiences based on profile, history, and preferences.

---

## HTTPS / WebSocket

Provides secure HTTPS communication and real-time bidirectional streaming using WebSockets.

---

# ZONE 2 — SECURITY & API ACCESS

## CDN (Static Assets / Edge Caching)

Caches static content like images, CSS, and JavaScript closer to users for faster performance and lower latency.

---

## API Gateway

Central entry point for all APIs that handles routing, authentication, throttling, monitoring, and request transformation.

---

## Authentication

Verifies user identity using SSO, OAuth2, OpenID Connect, JWT, or enterprise identity providers.

---

## WAF (Web Application Firewall)

Protects applications from attacks such as SQL Injection, XSS, CSRF, bots, and DDoS threats.

---

## Rate Limiter / Usage Quota / Logging

Controls API consumption, enforces quotas, and captures logs for monitoring, analytics, and auditing.

---

# ZONE 3A — CONVERSATIONAL AI RUNTIME

## Conversation Manager (Memory / History / State)

Maintains chat history, user context, session state, and long-term conversational memory.

---

## Web PubSub (WebSocket)

Enables real-time streaming of AI responses, notifications, and bidirectional communication.

---

## Service Bus

Supports asynchronous messaging and event-driven communication between distributed services.

---

## Agent Orchestrator

Coordinates AI agents, tools, workflows, and execution pipelines across the platform.

---

## Planner

Breaks user requests into tasks and determines execution strategy and workflow sequence.

---

## Router

Routes requests to the appropriate AI agent, tool, model, or service.

---

## Executor

Executes actions, workflows, tool calls, and orchestration steps defined by the planner.

---

## RAG Pipeline (Retrieval Augmented Generation)

Enhances LLM responses by retrieving relevant enterprise data and contextual knowledge.

---

## SQL + API + Data Access + Vector Search Engine

Provides unified access to databases, APIs, documents, files, and semantic/vector search systems.

---

# ZONE 3B — AI INSIGHTS & REPORTING RUNTIME

## Web PubSub (WebSocket)

Streams real-time insights, dashboards, alerts, and analytics updates to users.

---

## Service Bus

Handles asynchronous report processing, notifications, and event-driven insight generation.

---

## Report Stream Processing / KPI Aggregation / Metrics

Processes streaming business data and calculates KPIs, trends, and analytical metrics.

---

## Insight Analyzer (LLM)

Uses LLMs to analyze trends, summarize reports, detect anomalies, and generate business insights.

---

## Report & Alert Generator (PDF Reports / Email)

Automatically generates reports, dashboards, notifications, and email alerts.

---

# ZONE 4 — LLM GATEWAY

## Prompt Manager

Manages prompt templates, versions, governance, and prompt lifecycle management.

---

## Prompts

Reusable enterprise prompts optimized for different AI use cases and workflows.

---

## Context Builder

Constructs AI context using RAG results, user memory, metadata, APIs, and session information.

---

## Input Guardrails

Validates and filters unsafe or malicious prompts before they reach the LLM.

---

## Output Guardrails

Checks generated responses for safety, policy compliance, hallucinations, and restricted content.

---

## PII Masking

Detects and masks sensitive information such as SSNs, credit card numbers, and personal data.

---

## Model Registry / Router

Maintains available AI models and intelligently routes requests to the best model endpoint.

---

## Failover / Degradation

Provides high availability through backup models, graceful degradation, and resiliency mechanisms.

---

## GPT-4 / Claude / LLM Providers

External or internal large language model providers used for AI generation and reasoning.

---

# ZONE 5A — KNOWLEDGE / VECTOR LAYER

## Embedding Store

Stores vector embeddings for semantic search, retrieval, and contextual AI operations.

---

## Document Chunks

Splits large documents into smaller searchable chunks for efficient retrieval and grounding.

---

## User Context

Stores user preferences, memory, personalization data, and interaction history.

---

## Knowledge Base

Enterprise repository containing policies, manuals, FAQs, business knowledge, and documents.

---

# ZONE 5B — ENTERPRISE DATA & ANALYTICS

## Object Store / Blob (Raw Files)

Stores raw enterprise files, datasets, documents, images, logs, and AI training data.

---

## Redis / Cache

Provides high-speed caching for sessions, prompts, AI responses, and low-latency lookups.

---

## Data Warehouse / Semantic Models / Feature Store

Centralized enterprise analytics layer for BI reporting, semantic models, ML features, and AI insights.

---

# ZONE 6 — OBSERVABILITY & GOVERNANCE

## LLM Observability

Tracks prompts, token usage, latency, traces, hallucinations, feedback, and AI performance metrics.

---

## Infrastructure Metrics

Monitors infrastructure health, CPU, memory, network, errors, uptime, and system performance.

---

## Security & Audit

Captures audit logs, access tracking, compliance records, and security monitoring activities.

---

# ZONE 7 — DEVOPS & DEPLOYMENT

## CI/CD Pipeline

Automates application build, testing, deployment, and release management processes.

---

## IaC (Terraform) + AI Infra Environments

Uses Infrastructure as Code to provision, manage, and automate cloud and AI environments.

---

# END-TO-END FLOW DEFINITIONS

## Step 1 — User asks question in Web App

User interacts with AI through chat, dashboards, or applications.

---

## Step 2 — Request goes through API Gateway

Request is authenticated, validated, secured, and routed to backend services.

---

## Step 3 — AI Runtime processes & orchestrates

AI orchestration layer determines workflows, tools, and execution logic.

---

## Step 4 — RAG retrieves relevant context

Relevant enterprise documents and semantic search results are retrieved.

---

## Step 5 — LLM Gateway builds prompt & applies safety

Prompt is enriched with context and validated through safety guardrails.

---

## Step 6 — LLM generates response

Selected AI model generates the final response or insight.

---

## Step 7 — Insights / Reports / Alerts (Optional)

Platform generates analytics, dashboards, alerts, or summaries.

---

## Step 8 — Observability logs & monitors

System captures telemetry, metrics, audit logs, and governance information.
